  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nPartly cloudy skies will prevail behind a cold front today after\nany early morning showers end. Developing upslope flow will \nresult in mainly cloudy skies across the mountains. High \ntemperatures will range from the 50s across the north with 60s \nfurther to the south. West-northwest wind gusts may approach 30 \nmph during the afternoon. Tonight will be cooler with CAA \ncontinuing as overnight lows fall into the 20s and 30s. Dry \nconditions are expected this weekend with warming temperatures\nSunday and especially Monday.\n\nMainly dry conditions are likely to persist through at least the\nmiddle of next week with fluctuating temperatures, although it\nwill generally be warmer than avg. The next chance for any\nmeaningful rainfall may come at the end of the week as we\npotentially get into a pattern where richer moisture gets pulled\nnorthward ahead of a potentially deep trough.",
